Here’s the shortest path for others to run it locally:
Prerequisites
Node.js 18+ and npm
macOS/Windows/Linux
Setup
Clone:
git clone https://github.com/<username>/<repo>.git
cd DBMS
Install dependencies:
npm install
Initialize database:
npm run init-db
(Optional) Set env:
Create .env with JWT_SECRET=any-strong-secret (server has a default if omitted)
Run
Start server:
npm start
Open:
http://localhost:3000
Login/Test
Admin: admin@cms.com / admin123
Create a customer: http://localhost:3000/user-register.html
Track sample: CMS001 (from init data)
